 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Part three. The nails on the hatch *bend* like wire.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Sam and Jess run out the back door into the snow.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The car is buried to the windows. Sam digs with his hands.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Jess looks back at the house, and freezes.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "In the tiny attic window, something *tall* is standing.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Too tall for a man. Its head touches the roof beams.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "It raises one long arm, and *waves* at them.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Stay, because the snow stopped falling right then.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The engine starts on the third try. They drive until the road ends.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The sheriff finds them at dawn, at the closed bridge.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "When they say the address, he takes off his hat.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "The last owner ran from that house in 1984.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "He said someone walked in the attic, and repeated his words.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "That morning, the sheriff checks the attic with two deputies.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "They find an old mattress, candle wax, and a *notebook*.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every page is their routine. What they ate. When they slept.",
   "pausa": 0.5
  },
  {
   "texto": "And outside, fresh footprints lead *away* from the house, to Sam's car.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "If the snow shows prints coming in, count the ones going out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
